    "text_full": " \nHey, I'm Ben!\n\nI’ve been designing and developing websites for two decades. I’m currently a Senior Software Engineer at Zillow. Outside of my day job I build all kinds of web apps, art installations, furniture, and embedded electronics. I also host the hit podcast Cheese & Weather 🧀 🌩️ with Zuzana Kunckova and Dave Hicking.\n\nThe Kilopixel\n\nI spent 6 years building a ridiculous 1000-pixel display called the kilopixel. I let the internet draw on it and livestreamed 24/7 for a couple of weeks, and it's probably the most popular and wide-reaching thing I've ever put on the internet. I wrote an in-depth recap about the experience, which was pretty surreal!\n\nThe Pair-amid Scheme\n\nIn April 2024 I kicked off an experiment: pairing with strangers. It's morphed into The Pair-amid Scheme (h/t Joe) and I've paired with dozens of new friends from around the world.\n\nI highly recommend putting yourself out there and pairing with a random person from the internet! I think you'll be surprised by the results. If you need a kick start, feel free to book a spot on my calendar and I'll get you started.\n\nPopular Posts\nThe Kilopixel recap - season one\nI spent 6 years building a ridiculous wooden pixel display\nPairing with Strangers (the Pair-amid Scheme)\nMapping a Hyper key on MacOS with Karabiner Elements (the easy way)\nDefragment your PHPUnit tests\nRecent Posts\nA photo a day for 30 days\nBuilding howtall.is\nThe Art of Pairing with Strangers - Over Engineered Podcast\nJust how old is a 45 year old soup (and would you eat it)\nGrowing Into a Leadership Role, and Pairing With Strangers - The Business of Laravel Podcast\nVIEW ALL ⇢"
